# From the post of 2022-01-23 (studies/data/notes/post-abraham-justified-by-faith-james-2.html), in the author's words.

=== James 2
--- Abraham saved by faith alone, and James 2 [title]
overline: A post from the channel
heading: Abraham saved by faith alone, and James 2
sub: Abraham was saved by faith alone.
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the slides. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

--- Don't get me wrong
p: And please don't get me wrong, James 2 is an incredibly important lesson in how we as Christians should carry ourselves and use our faith to be effective for others through our works.
p: It's also crucial when understanding how others perceive us and that they are respecters of persons even though God isn't, and we shouldn't be.
p: It's also brilliant in how it's written, showing the Spirit of God in the words, framing the rhetorical question of what a man might say to a Christian to illustrate the points.

=== Faith alone
--- Saved by faith alone
lead: But of course we know from scripture that Abraham was saved by faith alone, and wasn't justified or made righteous by his works decades later, willing to sacrifice Isaac, long after he accepted the Lord and called upon his name for salvation.
p: We know this from reading the old testament, but more so we know it from the examples Paul uses regarding this in his Epistles.

--- Genesis 15:6 in Romans 4
p: Quoting Genesis 15:6
big: Genesis 15:6
p: in Romans 4:3-5:
scripture: Romans 4:3-5

--- The interpretation must be wrong
p: So, if these clear contradictions of the [[James 2:20|"faith without works is dead"]] interpretation can't be wrong, and if the snippet of out of context lines from James 2 cannot be wrong, then the interpretation, that James is saying Abraham wasn't saved until he was justified before God by his works instead of before man, must be wrong.
p: This is made evident in simply reading the full James 2 epistle and understand what's being talked about, and comparing scripture with scripture, the litany of verses explaining the Gospel is by faith alone in Christ to justify us, and accept God's forgiveness and eternal life, given in Grace, in return for that faith.

--- Because it is a gift
lead: Even he who worketh not...
p: Because it is a gift.
big: Ephesians 2:9

=== Only Jesus saves
--- Listen to me
lead: Listen to me when I tell you that if your preacher priest or pastor is teaching you that you need to do works in order to be saved, they are lying to you to control you and to keep you from the knowledge of the Gospel of the Lord.

--- Only Jesus saves
lead: Only Jesus saves, and he doesn't need our help for that.
p: He does need our help in winning souls to Christ that can only be done by those who are redeemed in his blood and who have accepted him as their only means of salvation without works. His work alone perfect. Complete.
p: If he is adding to that salvation with extra steps? Run. Then fall to your knees and call upon Christ alone to redeem you.

--- Any other gospel [title]
heading: Any other gospel
big: Galatians 1:8
read: app:doctrine-salvation | Salvation by grace through faith
